# Main functionality

The core endpoint should conceptually be:

```text
POST /jobs/ping
```

with a URL such as:

```text
https://example.com
```

The endpoint should enqueue a Celery task rather than performing the HTTP request itself.

Conceptually:

```text
POST /jobs/ping
       ↓
FastAPI receives URL
       ↓
Celery task is queued
       ↓
API returns task ID
       ↓
Redis transports task
       ↓
Celery worker executes task
       ↓
httpx performs HTTP GET
       ↓
result returned
```

OpenTelemetry should observe the relevant parts of this flow.

---

# Important OpenTelemetry goal

The most important thing I am trying to learn is **context propagation across process boundaries**.

I want to understand how something like:

```text
Trace ID: ABC123
```

can conceptually follow:

```text
FastAPI request
      ↓
Celery task submission
      ↓
Redis
      ↓
Celery worker
      ↓
HTTPX request
```

while the individual operations have different span IDs.

If automatic Celery instrumentation handles propagation, explain how it works conceptually.

If manual propagation is required anywhere, explain:

* why
* where the context is extracted
* where it is injected
* what `traceparent` represents

Do not simply make it work without explaining the mechanism.

